, Matt. 1:12); called also the son of Pedaiah (1 Chr. 3:17-19), i.e., according to a frequent usage of the word “son;” the grandson or the nephew of Salathiel.","verses":27,"father":"Pedaiah","mother":"","v":[2,14,16]},{"id":"joshua_893","name":"Joshua","also":"Jeshua","summary":"The son of Jozadak, and high priest of the Jews under Zerubbabel (Neh. 7:7; 12:1, 7, 10, 26); called Joshua (Hag. 1:1, 12; 2:2, 4; Zech. 3:1, 3, 6, 8, 9).","verses":21,"father":"Josedech","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"josedech_815","name":"Josedech","also":"Jozadak, Jehozadak","summary":"Jehovah-justified, the son of the high priest Seraiah at the time of the Babylonian exile (1 Chr. 6:14, 15). He was carried into captivity by Nebuchadnezzar, and probably died in Babylon.","verses":12,"father":"Seraiah","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"shealtiel_2456","name":"Shealtiel","also":"Salathiel","summary":"Asked for of God, father of Zerubbabel (Ezra 3:2, 8; Neh. 12:1).","verses":11,"father":"Jehoiachin","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"shethar-boznai_2674","name":"Shethar-boznai","also":"","summary":"Star of splendour, a Persian officer who vainly attempted to hinder the rebuilding of the temple (Ezra 5:3, 6; 6:6, 13).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,6]},{"id":"tatnai_2831","name":"Tatnai","also":"","summary":"Gift, a Persian governor (Heb. pehah, i.e., “satrap;” modern “pasha”) “on this side the river”, i.e., of the whole tract on the west of the Euphrates.","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,6]},{"id":"darius_978","name":"Darius","also":"","summary":"King of Persia.","verses":16,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,6,7]},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar_2167","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","also":"Nebuchadrezzar","summary":"In the Babylonian orthography Nabu-kudur-uzur, which means “Nebo, protect the crown!” or the “frontiers.” In an inscription he styles himself “Nebo’s favourite.”","verses":88,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12,14]},{"id":"cyrus_968","name":"Cyrus","also":"","summary":"(Heb. Ko’resh), the celebrated “King of Persia” (Elam) who was conqueror of Babylon, and issued the decree of liberation to the Jews (Ezra 1:1, 2).","verses":19,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,14,17]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,2,14,15,16,17]},{"id":"river_244","name":"river","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"region","verses":16,"v":[3,6]},{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[12,13,14,17]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[5029,5029,5029,2292,2148,2148,1247,5714,5714,5013,5922,3062,3062,3061,3061,3390,3390,8036,8036,8036,426,426,426,3479,3479,5922,5922,5922,5922],[116,2217,1247,7598,7598,3443,3443,1247,3136,3136,6966,6966,8271,8271,1124,1124,1005,1005,426,426,3390,3390,5029,5029,5029,1768,426,5974,5974,5974,5583,0],[2166,2166,2166,8674,6347,6347,5675,5675,5675,5675,5103,5103,5103,8370,3675,3675,3675,858,5922,5922,5922,560,560,4479,7761,7761,1124,1124,1836,1005,3635,3635,1836,846],[116,116,560,4479,581,8036,8036,1400,1400,1400,1768,1124,1124,1836,1147],[5870,5870,5870,426,426,426,1934,5922,7868,7868,3062,3062,3062,3809,3809,3809,3809,3809,989,5705,2941,2941,1946,1946,1868,1868,116,5407,5407,5922,1836,1836,8421,8421],[6573,6573,6573,6573,104,104,104,1768,8674,6347,6347,5675,5675,5675,5675,5103,5103,5103,8370,3675,3675,3675,671,671,5675,5675,5675,7972,5922,4430,1868],[6600,6600,7972,7972,5922,3790,3790,3790,4430,4430,1868,3606,8001],[1934,1934,1934,3046,4430,4430,4430,1768,236,236,4083,4083,4083,3061,3061,1005,1005,1005,7229,7229,7229,426,1932,1932,1124